.SH "نام (NAME)"
libnbd\-release\-notes\-1.20 \- release notes for libnbd 1.20
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
These are the release notes for libnbd stable release 1.20.
This describes the major changes since 1.18.
.PP
libnbd 1.20.0 was released on \fB5 April 2024\fR.
.SS Security
.IX Subsection "Security"
Fuzzing found and Eric Blake fixed an assertion which could be
triggered by connecting to a malicious server.  This was assigned
CVE\-2023\-5871 (low severity).  See the announcement here:
https://lists.libguestfs.org/archives/list/guestfs@lists.libguestfs.org/thread/5CRC7LRTN35WPZZ4BT6NAMH4JGMF47IK/
.PP
If you find a security issue, please read \fISECURITY\fR in the source
(online here:
https://gitlab.com/nbdkit/libnbd/blob/master/SECURITY).  To
find out about previous security issues in libnbd, see
\&\fBlibnbd\-security\fR\|(3).
.SS "Enhancements to existing APIs"
.IX Subsection "Enhancements to existing APIs"
\&\fBnbd_connect_uri\fR\|(3) now correctly supports case insensitive URIs.
.SS Protocol
.IX Subsection "Protocol"
Improve interop with \fBnbd\-server\fR\|(1) which supports structured
replies but not meta context (Eric Blake).
.SS Tools
.IX Subsection "Tools"
\&\fBnbdinfo\fR\|(1) adds support for \fI\-\-isnt\fR, \fI\-\-cannot\fR, \fI\-\-hasnt\fR,
which lets you check if features of an NBD server are \fInot\fR
supported.
.PP
\&\fBnbdinfo\fR\|(1) adds support for \fI\-\-uri\fR which just prints the
canonical URI of the server.
.PP
\&\fBnbdinfo\fR\|(1) now prints human sizes for block size constraints (Eric
Blake).
.SS "Language bindings"
.IX Subsection "Language bindings"
New \fBlibnbd\-rust\fR\|(3) manual page added, providing an overview for
writing Rust programs using libnbd.
.PP
Rust documentation has been improved by using a custom translator from
our own documentation format (Perl POD) to rustdoc.
.PP
Some Rust compiler warnings were fixed (Eric Blake).
.PP
OCaml bindings now support zero\-copy in AIO pread and pwrite
functions.  This change is backwards compatible with existing code.
(Thanks Nicolas Ojeda Bar, Anil Madhavapeddy, Simon Cruanes).
.PP
OCaml bindings now use \f(CW\*(C`Gc.finalize\*(C'\fR (OCaml\-level finalizers instead
of C\-level finalizers) which improves compatibility in OCaml 5.1.1 and
above (Guillaume Munch\-Maccagnoni).
.PP
OCaml ≥ 4.05 is formally required and checked in \fI./configure\fR.
Previously we did not specify a minimum version of OCaml, but in
practice versions older than 4.05 probably didn\*(Aqt work.
.SS Tests
.IX Subsection "Tests"
Fuzzing approach was changed to use asynchronous commands.  This
improves speed of fuzzing greatly and should find more issues.
.PP
Multiple CI fixes (Eric Blake).
.PP
Respect the user\*(Aqs choice of qemu\-nbd, nbdkit and other binaries from
(eg) \f(CW\*(C`./configure\ NBDKIT=/some/nbdkit\*(C'\fR.  Previously we would often
test against binaries found on the path even if the user had specified
other binaries to use.
.SS "Other improvements and bug fixes"
.IX Subsection "Other improvements and bug fixes"
\&\fBnbdinfo\fR\|(1) now gracefully disconnects from the server in error
cases, improving output (Eric Blake).
.PP
\&\f(CW\*(C`struct nbd_handle\*(C'\fR now contains a magic value which is checked on
entry to libnbd, which should identify mistakes where programs calling
libnbd pass in an incorrect pointer.
.SS Documentation
.IX Subsection "Documentation"
An example was added of how to use userfaultfd to mmap an NBD\-backed
drive.  See \fIexamples/userfault\-map.c\fR in the libnbd sources.
.PP
Documentation of acceptable handle states in the man pages has been
improved.
.SS Build
.IX Subsection "Build"
\&\fIcontrib/libnbd.m4\fR is a contributed configure test for libnbd (Bruno
Haible).
.PP
\&\f(CW\*(C`./configure \-\-with\-bash\-completions\*(C'\fR will now fail if the required
bash\-completions package is not installed.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBlibnbd\fR\|(3).
